CORE
nested_loop_flag1.sv
--bound 0
^\[main\.p0\] always .*: PROVED up to bound 0$
^\[main\.p1\] always .*: PROVED up to bound 0$
^\[main\.p2\] always main\.ok -> main\.used == 255: PROVED up to bound 0$
^\[main\.p3\] always main\.ok -> main\.w\[0\] == main\.rdata\[7:0\]: REFUTED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
Each iteration of the nested loop reads back and conditionally updates
'found' and 'used'. The RTL builder must name the intermediate values
to avoid exponential growth (https://github.com/diffblue/hw-cbmc/issues/2196).
